# Job description text is the employer's copyrighted content, and naming every
# posting you apply to is not something to publish. Keep it local.
jd.txt
jd*.txt
*.jd.txt
job-description*
postings/

# One folder per application: the posting, edit set, and tailored resumes. The
# folders are the archive of past applications - see docs/adr/0001.
applications/

# The Experience ledger: what the user confirmed or denied in past consultations.
# Tokens only, but it is still a private record of their background.
experience.md

# The real identity values behind canon's [Token]s, read only by `fill`. This
# is the file the whole placeholder scheme exists to keep out of git, and a
# PreToolUse hook blocks Claude from reading it at all.
pii.txt
pii*.txt

# NEVER commit a resume with the placeholders filled in - real name, email,
# phone, employers. Git history is permanent; a PII leak here cannot be undone
# by a later delete. Fill tokens in a copy that matches one of these names.
*_filled.*
*_final.*
*_submitted.*
*-filled.*
private/

# The name tailored outputs are filed under. Real name, so it stays local.
.output_name

# Canon is the user's own resume, not part of this tool. It stays local, and a
# fresh clone is expected to arrive without one - the skill aborts and asks.
# The preview is LibreOffice output, regenerable from canon at any time.
canon_resume.odt
canon_resume*.odt
canon_resume_preview.pdf

# Don't commit generated resume and report
*_Resume.odt
*_ATS_Report.md

# Per-job edit set fed to `apply`. Quotes canon's bullets verbatim, same reason
# migration/ is kept out below - regenerated fresh each run anyway.
edits.json

# Edit sets that built canon. They quote its bullets verbatim, so committing
# them would publish in fragments the document canon is kept out of git to avoid.
migration/

# LibreOffice lock files and Python bytecode
.~lock.*#
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Scratch renders
/render-*/
*.tmp

.vscode
